  the Gregorian calendar.  רֹאשׁ חוֹדֶשׁ\, transliterated Rosh 
 Chodesh or Rosh Hodesh\, is a minor holiday that occurs at the beginning o
 f every month in the Hebrew calendar. It is marked by the birth of a new m
 oon\n\nTorah: Numbers 28:1-15
